WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.158
Their perfect work makes you see only your erasures?

00:00:03.158 --> 00:00:06.316
Comparison can quietly change the reference point.

00:00:06.316 --> 00:00:09.474
Social comparison examines self-evaluation.

00:00:09.474 --> 00:00:12.632
The target and dimension both matter.

00:00:12.632 --> 00:00:15.789
The same gap can prompt different feelings.

00:00:15.789 --> 00:00:22.105
You see the finished work, not all the practice.

00:00:22.105 --> 00:00:28.421
Your process meets someone else’s display window.

00:00:28.421 --> 00:00:34.737
Unequal information may magnify the felt gap.

00:00:34.737 --> 00:00:41.053
This mirror represents the comparison process.

00:00:41.053 --> 00:00:44.211
This does not mean every display is false.

00:00:44.211 --> 00:00:47.368
A different comparison does not guarantee relief.

00:00:47.368 --> 00:00:50.526
Goals, relationships and context also matter.

00:00:50.526 --> 00:00:56.842
Ask what method the artwork can teach.

00:00:56.842 --> 00:01:03.158
Compare one specific change with your own past.

00:01:03.158 --> 00:01:06.316
Take space from the display when useful.

00:01:06.316 --> 00:01:09.474
Another person’s strength can offer a clue.

00:01:09.474 --> 00:01:12.632
Your worth is wider than one comparison.

00:01:12.632 --> 00:01:15.789
Return your attention to one doable step.
